@title Lede Format

# Lede

### A line-oriented document format for AI-written web artifacts. Compiles to HTML.

> One line is one block. Indentation never matters. The compiler owns the design.

Markdown can't carry data, charts or diagrams. HTML can, but the model spends most of its output on styling and structure instead of content. Lede sits between them: the writer states **what** to show, and the compiler decides **how** it looks, in light and dark, at phone and desktop widths.

kpi Source on this page | 3.1 KB
kpi Compiled HTML | 17.4 KB | 5.7× larger
kpi Block types | 14

## The rules

- Every line starts with what it is: `#`, `-`, `!`, `>`, or a keyword like `chart` or `diagram`.
- Nothing nests and nothing needs closing, so a model can stream it and a parser can render it mid-generation.
- Data is declared once with `data`, then charts and tables reference it by name.
- Diagram lines are prefixed with the diagram's name, so they can appear anywhere after it.
- `html:` is the escape hatch for anything the vocabulary doesn't cover.

## A whole section, as written

```
data runs = week,deploys,rollbacks; W1,14,2; W2,19,1; W3,23,3; W4,31,1
chart line runs x=week y=deploys,rollbacks title="Deploys per week"
table runs sort=-deploys

diagram flow dir=LR
flow: commit -> build -> test -> deploy : on green
flow: deploy "Prod" svc
```

## Charts

data runs = week,deploys,rollbacks; W1,14,2; W2,19,1; W3,23,3; W4,31,1; W5,28,2; W6,36,1; W7,41,0; W8,44,1
chart line runs x=week y=deploys,rollbacks title="Deploys per week (sample data)"

data size = format,KB; Lede source,3.1; HTML body,11.9; Full page,17.4
chart bar size x=format y=KB title="This page, measured"

table runs sort=-deploys limit=4 title="Busiest weeks"

## Diagrams

Diagrams are laid out by Graphviz, the same engine behind Python's `diagrams` package, then drawn by the compiler in the page's own type and colors. Kinds like `svc`, `db` and `queue` set the color and a small label.

diagram pipeline dir=TB title="How the compiler works"
pipeline: src ".lede source" user
pipeline: lex "Line classifier" fn
pipeline: data "Data registry" store
pipeline: gv "Graphviz layout" ext
pipeline: emit "HTML + theme" svc
pipeline: src -> lex
pipeline: lex -> data : data
pipeline: lex -> gv : diagram
pipeline: data -> emit : chart, table
pipeline: gv -> emit : svg coords
pipeline: lex -> emit : text blocks

Groups draw dashed boundaries, which covers accounts, VPCs and regions:

diagram ca dir=TB title="CodeArtifact org registry"
ca: dev "Developer" user
ca: npm "npmjs.com" ext
ca: team-dev "team-repo (dev)" db
ca: team-prod "team-repo (prod)" db
ca: shared "shared-org-repo" db
ca: upstream "npm-store" db
ca: group "Producer accounts" team-dev, team-prod
ca: group "Shared prod account" shared, upstream
ca: team-dev -> team-prod : promote
ca: team-prod -> shared : copy
ca: npm -> upstream -> shared : upstream
ca: shared -> dev : pull (org policy)

## Callouts and quotes

! Notes use one bang. Warnings use two.
!! Diagram blocks need Graphviz `dot` on the machine that compiles.

---

Compile with `python3 lede.py page.lede > page.html`.
